WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.580 --> 00:00:04.910
The Dark Knight has got his darkest movie
yet, with a villain more in common with the

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:06.950
Jigsaw killer than Jim Carrey.

00:00:06.950 --> 00:00:12.570
Bruce Wayne goes to some bleak places in "The
Batman" – and these are his darkest depths.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:16.180
By the time "The Batman" starts, it's been
two years since Bruce Wayne's mission to fight

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:20.430
crime in Gotham has begun — and by his own
admission, he's failing.

00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:23.740
Things have only gotten worse since he put
on the mask and began spending his nights

00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:26.150
striking fear into the hearts of criminals.

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:29.650
Even though the myth of The Batman and the
looming threat of the violence he spreads

00:00:29.650 --> 00:00:33.430
has rattled the criminal element, it has barely
slowed their pace.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:37.430
Bruce wants to change Gotham for the better,
but knows deep down that what he is doing

00:00:37.430 --> 00:00:39.830
is not having its intended effect.

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:43.850
Before he can fix his focus on the bigger
picture and discover the true breadth of corruption

00:00:43.850 --> 00:00:48.440
and graft that has long strangled any potential
for improvement in Gotham, he must trudge

00:00:48.440 --> 00:00:52.720
through this fruitless, repetitive cycle – and
by the time we meet him, it's clear that it's

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:54.230
taking a toll.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:59.040
The first time we see Batman in action, the
audience gets a glimpse of what these brutal

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.780
late nights have been like for Bruce.

00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:05.330
He encounters a gang of face-painted hoods,
recreationally assaulting random people in

00:01:05.330 --> 00:01:07.010
the street and filming it for kicks.

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:11.050
They're about to descend on their latest victim,
a guy simply trying to make it home on the

00:01:11.050 --> 00:01:15.250
train, when they are confronted by Batman
in full, cloaked regalia.

00:01:15.250 --> 00:01:17.480
"I'm vengeance."

00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:22.050
On some level, it's a thrilling action scene;
on another, it's a discomforting example of

00:01:22.050 --> 00:01:24.570
Bruce's flawed approach to fixing his city.

00:01:24.570 --> 00:01:28.480
He dispenses with the gang members despite
being outnumbered, but takes significant damage

00:01:28.480 --> 00:01:29.930
himself in the process.

00:01:29.930 --> 00:01:33.160
Shot at, tasered, kicked, punched, hit with
weapons?

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.590
No amount of billionaire armor and gadgetry
is going to fully soften those blows.

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:42.800
It's almost like he has a masochistic streak,
believing he deserves such nightly beatdowns.

00:01:42.800 --> 00:01:47.690
The ferocity it takes to overcome those odds
and fight the gang showcases the sort of monster

00:01:47.690 --> 00:01:48.920
Bruce has become.

00:01:48.920 --> 00:01:53.590
The innocent bystander he set out to save
from the face-paint gang is far from appreciative,

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:57.020
cowering under the Batman's gaze out of fear
that he'll be next.

00:01:57.020 --> 00:02:01.010
The carnage on display makes it hard for him
to comprehend that Bruce is a good guy – which

00:02:01.010 --> 00:02:05.150
makes you wonder what exactly Bruce Wayne
is getting out of all of this.

00:02:05.150 --> 00:02:09.640
By virtue of being the only living soul who
knows Bruce's secret, Alfred is burdened with

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.850
a sense of objectivity that Bruce is sorely
lacking.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:16.950
Every night Bruce comes home to the cave and
throws himself into maintaining his case files,

00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:19.380
diaries and ongoing investigations.

00:02:19.380 --> 00:02:23.530
It's Alfred – the closest thing Bruce has
to a father – who has to perform the unfortunate

00:02:23.530 --> 00:02:27.810
task of pointing out the ineffective, unsustainable
nature of his efforts.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:32.860
But, like many who love a person with self-destructive
tendencies, he still tries to be supportive.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:37.440
Much like it was the case with Christian Bale's
Batman, it's Bruce's responses and reactions

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:41.410
to real concerns that make these early morning
reality checks so depressing.

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:44.080
"Oh, you know how it is Mr. Fox.

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:49.260
You're out at night, looking for kicks, someone's
passing around weaponized hallucinogens."

00:02:49.260 --> 00:02:52.790
We've already established through Bruce's
own admission that he doesn't really care

00:02:52.790 --> 00:02:54.440
if he dies doing what he's doing.

00:02:54.440 --> 00:02:58.460
But when Alfred urges him to think of his
family's legacy, as he continues to ignore

00:02:58.460 --> 00:03:02.739
managing his fortune or engaging with the
company his father left him, Bruce remarks

00:03:02.739 --> 00:03:06.239
that his mission as The Batman is his family's
legacy.

00:03:06.239 --> 00:03:10.680
That alone would be a pretty dark declaration
to make, but every time Alfred pushes him

00:03:10.680 --> 00:03:15.190
further, Bruce responds with callous and selfish
thoughts to put Alfred in his place.

00:03:15.190 --> 00:03:19.930
When Alfred tries to be firm, Bruce reminds
Alfred he's his butler and not his father.

00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:23.550
When Alfred won't let Bruce go to a funeral
without cufflinks on, to keep up appearances,

00:03:23.550 --> 00:03:28.770
he makes Bruce wear his own, to which Bruce
asks if Alfred himself is a Wayne.

00:03:28.770 --> 00:03:32.910
It's a question whose answer is meant to hurt
Alfred for suggesting any connection to this

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:33.910
lineage.

00:03:33.910 --> 00:03:38.430
Alfred explains to Bruce that it was his Thomas
Wayne who gifted him the cufflinks, and that

00:03:38.430 --> 00:03:42.950
he was close enough to be family to the man
Bruce is killing himself every night to avenge.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:48.190
"The Batman" is a movie that, more than any
other Batman flick, showcases Bruce's intelligence

00:03:48.190 --> 00:03:49.989
and skill as a detective.

00:03:49.989 --> 00:03:53.599
But this being a story that takes place so
early in his career, it also highlights how

00:03:53.599 --> 00:03:54.980
fallible he is.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:59.190
Midway through unraveling the film's central
mystery behind who The Riddler is and what

00:03:59.190 --> 00:04:03.790
maze of moral rot he is trying to uncover
in Gotham's history, Bruce and Lieutenant

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:07.120
Gordon believe they have figured out who "the
rat" is.

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:11.620
The latest riddle they've solved references
an informant tethered to The Riddler's accusations

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:15.709
that there's rampant corruption both in the
Gotham City Police Department and the city's

00:04:15.709 --> 00:04:17.430
political power structure.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.739
Bruce believes the riddle refers, in broken
Spanish, to "a rat with wings," leading him

00:04:21.739 --> 00:04:26.460
to think it's The Penguin, the right hand
man to mob boss Carmine Falcone.

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:31.759
After an insane car chase, The Batman and
Gordon tag team Penguin with their key accusation,

00:04:31.759 --> 00:04:35.710
going back and forth like a pair of cops in
an interrogation, but Penguin insists he's

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:36.710
not the rat.

00:04:36.710 --> 00:04:40.860
When they repeat the riddle, which includes
the phrase "you are el rata alada" Penguin

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:45.330
points out that it should be "la" since the
noun in question is feminine.

00:04:45.330 --> 00:04:50.150
Bruce realizes the bit the Riddler emphasized
is "you are el" and types the rest of the

00:04:50.150 --> 00:04:53.900
phrase into a browser that leads to a chat
window with the Riddler.

00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:58.409
There he realizes Riddler's next victim is
Bruce Wayne, and desperately tries to race

00:04:58.409 --> 00:05:01.610
home to save Alfred from the bomb that's been
shipped there.

00:05:01.610 --> 00:05:03.139
But he arrives too late.

00:05:03.139 --> 00:05:08.309
Alfred is hospitalized and in critical condition
— all because Bruce misinterpreted a clue.

00:05:08.309 --> 00:05:12.543
"Oh, you're really not as smart as I thought
you were."

00:05:12.543 --> 00:05:13.543
Sins of the father

00:05:13.543 --> 00:05:16.990
As he probes more deeply into Gotham's history
and sees how crooked its vaunted power structures

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:21.889
have long been, he can accept that the shape
of his enemy is more sprawling and vast than

00:05:21.889 --> 00:05:23.270
he initially surmised.

00:05:23.270 --> 00:05:27.490
But when the Riddler exposes the hidden history
of Bruce Wayne's own family, it shakes him

00:05:27.490 --> 00:05:28.879
to his foundation.

00:05:28.879 --> 00:05:32.619
In this iteration of the story, the Waynes
were murdered not long after Thomas Wayne's

00:05:32.619 --> 00:05:34.370
bid for mayor of Gotham.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:38.539
The Riddler posits that the Waynes and the
other founding family of the city, the Arkhams,

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:43.249
had always exerted control over Gotham through
their power and wealth, but in no case was

00:05:43.249 --> 00:05:47.559
this more pernicious than when a reporter
was digging into their past during the campaign.

00:05:47.559 --> 00:05:52.020
A journalist uncovered that Martha, an Arkham
before she married into the Waynes, suffered

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:56.789
from severe mental illness in her youth and
had a lengthy stay in the asylum of her namesake.

00:05:56.789 --> 00:06:01.340
Thomas, worried the scandal would impact his
campaign, used his influence over Falcone,

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:05.889
having once saved the man's life, to get him
to silence the reporter — who was murdered.

00:06:05.889 --> 00:06:10.249
Suddenly faced with the realization that his
father wasn't the noble, altruistic victim

00:06:10.249 --> 00:06:15.139
he has committed himself to avenging, Bruce
is sent into a tailspin, calling into question

00:06:15.139 --> 00:06:16.610
everything he's ever known.

00:06:16.610 --> 00:06:20.259
Although he later discovers that what he's
been told by the Riddler and Falcone isn't

00:06:20.259 --> 00:06:26.009
exactly the whole story, such revelations
still rock him to the very core of his being.

00:06:26.009 --> 00:06:30.999
When the Riddler is revealed to be forensic
accountant Edward Nashton and put behind bars,

00:06:30.999 --> 00:06:34.840
Batman comes face to face with him, only to
discover some disturbing wrinkles to their

00:06:34.840 --> 00:06:36.490
adversarial relationship.

00:06:36.490 --> 00:06:39.879
Firstly, Bruce discovers Nashton knows who
he really is.

00:06:39.879 --> 00:06:44.210
He arrives to their little tête-à-tête
thinking his days of anonymity are over and

00:06:44.210 --> 00:06:48.560
that Nashton is going to reveal his identity,
but what he finds out is far worse.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:53.030
Nashton goes on a lengthy rant about how he
always resented the sympathy the city had

00:06:53.030 --> 00:06:57.259
for the poor little rich boy who lost his
parents, but not Nashton or the other orphans

00:06:57.259 --> 00:07:02.539
suffering in the dilapidated orphanage whose
funding had been pillaged by greedy bureaucrats.

00:07:02.539 --> 00:07:06.360
But beneath this screed about his motivations
is the revelation that his master plan is

00:07:06.360 --> 00:07:09.009
even larger than his string of killings.

00:07:09.009 --> 00:07:13.159
Batman comes to understand that the Riddler
views himself as a kindred spirit, the same

00:07:13.159 --> 00:07:15.899
kind of necessary vigilante as Batman.

00:07:15.899 --> 00:07:20.309
He sees the two of them, together, as partners,
as he's made Bruce an unwilling participant

00:07:20.309 --> 00:07:21.309
in his plans.

00:07:21.309 --> 00:07:25.789
Later, during a climactic showdown with one
of Riddler's followers, Bruce injects himself

00:07:25.789 --> 00:07:27.580
with some kind of adrenaline shot.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:31.839
It sends him into overdrive – he brutally
beats his opponent, nearly killing him.

00:07:31.839 --> 00:07:34.869
The man, near death, responds to the question
"who are you?"

00:07:34.869 --> 00:07:39.679
with a haunting answer – instead of being
straightforward, Batman's enemy says, "I'm

00:07:39.679 --> 00:07:42.969
vengeance," echoing Batman's very own words
right back at him.

00:07:42.969 --> 00:07:47.159
As rock-bottom as this moment might be for
Bruce, it's a necessary wake-up call.

00:07:47.159 --> 00:07:51.629
For as dark as "The Batman" is, it's a story
that must plumb those depths to come out the

00:07:51.629 --> 00:07:56.069
other side transformed, a Bruce Wayne who
understands that Gotham needs more than fear

00:07:56.069 --> 00:07:58.379
and violence to be saved from itself.

00:07:58.379 --> 00:07:59.379
It needs hope.

00:07:59.379 --> 00:08:01.250
And so does Bruce Wayne.

